CHUNK({"chunk":"Q","module":"m4","topics":[{"id":"m4-sustainable-development","title":"Sustainable development and the origin of the SDGs","short":"Sustainable development","blurb":"The meaning of sustainable development, its limits, poverty and equity, how the SDGs grew from Johannesburg and Rio+20, and why environment and development go together.","source":"Lecture W4 (Sustainable Development Goals), pages 1, 3–4","tabs":[{"title":"Meaning","html":"\n          <p class=\"lead\"><b>Sustainable development</b>: meets present needs <b>without compromising the ability of future generations</b> to meet theirs.</p>\n          <ul>\n            <li><b>Limits not absolute</b>: set by technology, social organisation, biosphere's absorbing capacity.</li>\n            <li>Endemic <b>poverty</b> invites ecological disasters; <b>equity</b> for the poor.</li>\n            <li>A <b>process of change</b>, not a fixed state of harmony.</li>\n            <li>Environment and development: <b>two sides of one agenda</b>.</li>\n          </ul>\n        "},{"title":"Genesis of SDGs, awareness","html":"\n          <ol class=\"steps\">\n            <li><b>Johannesburg</b> World Summit: <b>Johannesburg Plan of Implementation (JPOI)</b></li>\n            <li><b>2012</b>, <b>\"The Future We Want\"</b>: SDGs to build on <b>Agenda 21</b> + JPOI; <b>high-level political forum</b> replaced Commission for Sustainable Development</li>\n            <li><b>September 2015</b>: SDGs agreed at <b>UN, New York</b></li>\n          </ol>\n          <p>Awareness: main cause of ignorance <b>illiteracy</b>; key areas <b>agriculture, industry, health</b>; channels incl. <b>mass media</b>.</p>\n        "}],"flashcards":[{"front":"Define sustainable development.","back":"Meeting present needs without compromising future generations' ability to meet theirs."},{"front":"Are the limits of sustainable development absolute?","back":"<b>No</b>; set by current technology, social organisation and the biosphere's absorbing capacity."},{"front":"What was \"The Future We Want\"?","back":"The <b>2012</b> outcome document that committed states to build the SDGs."}],"cardCount":6,"formulaCount":0},{"id":"m4-sdgs","title":"The 17 Sustainable Development Goals","short":"The 17 SDGs","blurb":"All seventeen goals with their full aims, grouped so they are easier to remember.","source":"Lecture W4 (Sustainable Development Goals), page 2","tabs":[{"title":"Goals 1–9","html":"\n          <table class=\"tbl\">\n            <tbody>\n              <tr><td><b>1</b></td><td>No <b>poverty</b> in all forms</td></tr>\n              <tr><td><b>2</b></td><td>Zero <b>hunger</b>, food security, sustainable agriculture</td></tr>\n              <tr><td><b>3</b></td><td>Health, <b>well-being</b></td></tr>\n              <tr><td><b>4</b></td><td>Quality <b>education</b></td></tr>\n              <tr><td><b>5</b></td><td><b>Gender equality</b></td></tr>\n              <tr><td><b>6</b></td><td>Clean <b>water and sanitation</b></td></tr>\n              <tr><td><b>7</b></td><td>Affordable, clean <b>energy</b></td></tr>\n              <tr><td><b>8</b></td><td>Decent work, <b>economic growth</b></td></tr>\n              <tr><td><b>9</b></td><td><b>Infrastructure</b>, industry, innovation</td></tr>\n            </tbody>\n          </table>\n        "},{"title":"Goals 10–17","html":"\n          <table class=\"tbl\">\n            <tbody>\n              <tr><td><b>10</b></td><td>Reduced <b>inequality</b></td></tr>\n              <tr><td><b>11</b></td><td>Sustainable <b>cities</b></td></tr>\n              <tr><td><b>12</b></td><td><b>Consumption and production</b></td></tr>\n              <tr><td><b>13</b></td><td><b>Climate action</b></td></tr>\n              <tr><td><b>14</b></td><td><b>Life below water</b></td></tr>\n              <tr><td><b>15</b></td><td><b>Life on land</b> (forests, desertification)</td></tr>\n              <tr><td><b>16</b></td><td><b>Peace, justice</b>, institutions</td></tr>\n              <tr><td><b>17</b></td><td><b>Partnerships</b></td></tr>\n            </tbody>\n          </table>\n          <div class=\"note trap\">Goal <b>6</b> water for people vs Goal <b>14</b> oceans. Goal <b>13</b> climate vs Goal <b>15</b> forests.</div>\n        "}],"flashcards":[{"front":"How many SDGs are there?","back":"<b>17</b>."},{"front":"SDG 6?","back":"Clean <b>water and sanitation</b> for all."},{"front":"SDG 7?","back":"Affordable, clean <b>energy</b> for all."}],"cardCount":8,"formulaCount":0}],"figures":[]});
